0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BlogPosting\",\"headline\":\"GPA Requirements for College/University Admission? (2026)\",\"description\":\"Discover what GPA you need for college in 2026. We break down GPA requirements by university tier, weighted Vs. unweighted GPAs, and tips for every score range.\",\"image\":[\"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/djth6w3n/production/33e067bca85083405622df09b309ed74b185a991-1376x768.webp?rect=0,23,1376,722&w=1200&h=630&fit=crop&auto=format\"],\"datePublished\":\"2026-06-04T14:00:30.894Z\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-06-04T14:00:30.894Z\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://edutoolshub.com/blog/gpa-requirements-for-college-university-admission-2026\"},\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"EduToolsHub\",\"url\":\"https://edutoolshub.com\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"EduToolsHub\",\"url\":\"https://edutoolshub.com\"}}"}}],["$","$L2",null,{"post":{"_id":"f3704a5a-be46-437d-b159-44c853ec8c7f","body":[{"_key":"89d5f714d474","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"02bf24c2d882","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"GPA Requirements for College/University Admission? (2026)"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h1"},{"_key":"f4bf0b65e896","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"39396a18efd3","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"If you’re a high school student preparing college applications, you may ask early on: “Is my GPA high enough?” A reasonable worry exists. Your Grade Point Average is one of the most important parts of your application. Knowing what colleges truly look for can save you stress, doubt, and second-guessing."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"d8383a0462f4","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"b15c07123cbc","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"This guide breaks down GPA requirements across every tier of colleges and universities. In recent admissions cycles, it explains the difference between weighted and unweighted GPAs. It also gives practical steps, whether your GPA is strong, average, or needs work."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"efa72561c3de","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"28af9d310279","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Table of Contents"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h2"},{"_key":"07b586655bf2","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"d3fe0917bf62","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"What Is GPA and Why Does It Matter Most?"}],"level":1,"listItem":"number","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"6cfdc37fdc12","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"3131c03cb29b","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Weighted vs. Unweighted GPA"}],"level":1,"listItem":"number","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"9b53623c5531","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"15f8ae6f42ee","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Average College GPA Requirements by University Type"}],"level":1,"listItem":"number","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"351e0becb1ae","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"4727a65aa24c","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Minimum GPA vs Competitive GPA"}],"level":1,"listItem":"number","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"f435a99653b5","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"0449e0b58eea","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"How GPA Affects Admissions"}],"level":1,"listItem":"number","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"85616f4f3c08","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"044e792461f6","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Test-Optional Admissions and GPA"}],"level":1,"listItem":"number","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"3c24ba02f98d","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"f79bd292e89d","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"What If Your GPA Is Low?"}],"level":1,"listItem":"number","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"471978a67f49","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"236c38370c5b","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Common GPA Myths"}],"level":1,"listItem":"number","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"b19899cacdf6","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"1ba79407d932","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"How to Check GPA Requirements"}],"level":1,"listItem":"number","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"0fa2f58355d7","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"31e42e7a398e","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"FAQs"}],"level":1,"listItem":"number","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"aeee62122cf1","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"ce79d80b0fa3","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"What Is a GPA and Why Does It Matter Most?"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h2"},{"_key":"dd4216c79143","_type":"image","alt":"Grade Point Average Image","asset":{"_id":"image-5dda607fbc67aaf91ed823d8ced2d2f4585440dc-299x200-webp","metadata":{"dimensions":{"_type":"sanity.imageDimensions","aspectRatio":1.495,"height":200,"width":299},"lqip":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/djth6w3n/production/5dda607fbc67aaf91ed823d8ced2d2f4585440dc-299x200.webp"},"caption":"Grade Point Average","markDefs":null},{"_key":"00f6a6c8155f","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"a8b8a0156f27","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Your GPA is a number that sums up your high school academic performance. Schools calculate it on a 4.0 scale (unweighted) or a 5.0+ scale (weighted). Colleges use it as one of the first screening tools when reviewing your application."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"d17dd88c016a","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"720860186574","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"As one admissions expert puts it, your GPA is the ticket that gets you into the room. Once you are there, your essays, recommendations, and extracurriculars determine if you get a seat at the table."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"e8aa28dc5a73","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"52c71e20d67d","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"In recent admissions cycles, GPA carries more weight than ever. With top schools like Stanford, Harvard, and Yale bringing back test requirements, test-optional policies are ending. Admissions officers are now paying closer attention to GPA and test scores. They are focusing on these more than at any point in the past five years."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"72db9d0defe7","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"71fdf43ade15","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Weighted vs. Unweighted GPA: What Is the Difference?"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h2"},{"_key":"a0c8d23d96bd","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"41e758902321","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Before looking at specific numbers, you should understand that schools don’t all calculate GPAs the same way."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"4e7927944431","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"f560475f7c3f","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Unweighted GPA"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h3"},{"_key":"4f15ba44916a","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"9bc33689991c","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"An unweighted GPA is calculated on a standard 4.0 scale. The school treats every class equally, regardless of difficulty."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"59ba44f3a2a6","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"89e63af6f6a2","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"An A earns 4.0 points"}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"532299e5b0e0","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"cc577411776a","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"A B earns 3.0 points"}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"540da5c5ce7a","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"badaaf08571d","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"A C earns 2.0 points"}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"e8977e8eb1b2","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"dde76f467acb","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"A student who earns all A's in Advanced Placement (AP) classes also has a 4.0. The unweighted scale does not reward course difficulty."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"b5e835e1fb25","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"10da9c64a702","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Weighted GPA"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h3"},{"_key":"f4398152c0d2","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"f3b4d711dd6d","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"A weighted GPA accounts for course rigor by assigning extra point values to harder classes. Most weighted scales extend to 5.0, although a few reach higher levels."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"b9178e20653b","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"d4b335485c18","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"An A in an honors class typically earns 4.5 points"}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"27db35d01ce7","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"84bc02789ac8","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"An A in an AP or IB class typically earns 5.0 points"}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"81dd37debba4","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"4a9ff5e72258","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"This means a student taking challenging courses can have a weighted GPA that exceeds 4.0."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"5a65972b1433","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"bf48535f563d","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Which One Do Colleges Value?"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h3"},{"_key":"f9b1ee981387","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"149cfaa2de68","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"The most truthful response is both, but in different ways."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"eba6444cf3ef","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"063a909b46b9","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Most selective colleges recalculate your GPA using their own formula during application review. What they are **truly** looking for is a combination of strong grades and the most rigorous course load available to you at your school."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"3007cbbb8467","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"94e132cabe9d","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"A common myth is that colleges only look at weighted GPA. In reality, most selective schools use their own standard system. So, a high weighted GPA from easy classes will not impress a smart admissions officer."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"d82729314b01","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"9c504e4efb8e","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"In 2026, the average unweighted GPA for admitted students at the top ten universities is about 3.95. Weighted GPAs at those schools often exceed 4.4. Almost every successful applicant to elite schools gets mostly A’s."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"8cfbeb9541d9","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"c5efc63db34e","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"They earn these grades in the hardest classes available to them."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"adf19d568ca5","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"15f8ae6f42ee","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Average College GPA Requirements by University Type"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h2"},{"_key":"714361a7eb31","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"806b34163c8a","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Every college has different expectations. Here is a realistic breakdown of what you need depending on the type of school you are targeting."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"1babc07c12fd","_type":"image","alt":"students filling out the admission form","asset":{"_id":"image-9c2b0e55c43c8170f97f9aec79c96acf6d559eba-1408x768-webp","metadata":{"dimensions":{"_type":"sanity.imageDimensions","aspectRatio":1.8333333333333333,"height":768,"width":1408},"lqip":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/djth6w3n/production/9c2b0e55c43c8170f97f9aec79c96acf6d559eba-1408x768.webp"},"markDefs":null},{"_key":"e4b32345f0c8","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"d24d5e0205de","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Ivy League and Elite Private Universities"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h3"},{"_key":"c4007374b966","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"68b3f3cb739b","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"(Harvard, Yale, Princeton, Columbia, MIT, Stanford)"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"0c1f1281a5e5","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"71bb0bf7540d","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"These are the most competitive institutions in the country, and their GPA expectations reflect that."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"ed46f727a9a6","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"e13d7bf28634","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Recommended unweighted GPA: 3.9 or higher"}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"454217a09c1b","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"ade51a0295ff","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Average admitted student GPA: 3.95 to 4.0 unweighted; 4.4 or above weighted"}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"29f2e508daed","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"825e38d3d4b4","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"At Harvard, over 72% of admitted students have a perfect 4.0, and more than 22% have a GPA between 3.75 and 3.99"}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"13470f088935","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"ea104cf70b54","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"At Ivy League schools broadly, over 90% of admitted students have GPAs above 3.75"}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"e4de7147345d","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"349cce2b2566","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"MIT's average admitted GPA is approximately 4.17 on a weighted scale"}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"1c2b8cf1b26c","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"c84307e2e1ba","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"A high GPA alone does not guarantee admission to these schools. They seek consistent excellence."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"a079988d048d","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"9fec58a8f7d3","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"They prefer a student who kept a 3.9 GPA for all four years. They favor this more than a student who began poorly but improved afterward. They also place enormous weight on course rigor, extracurricular achievement, essays, and recommendation letters."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"40cd9a1df131","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"0db034c106d4","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Highly Selective National Universities"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h3"},{"_key":"f2ed6e106ad5","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"6b530ee126b8","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"(UCLA, UC Berkeley, University of Michigan, UNC Chapel Hill, Georgetown)"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"f8cbbf8c6891","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"fa1d0765ab74","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"These schools sit just below the Ivy League in selectivity, but are still fiercely competitive."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"a50aaaa91191","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"6c3583114bf3","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Recommended unweighted GPA: 3.7 to 3.9"}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"36db0dca3b0b","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"4b92bcff6a62","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"For the UC system (UCLA and UC Berkeley), the average GPA for admitted students in 2026 was 4.21 to 4.33 on a weighted scale"}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"e8bc15092622","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"5d0c736e61a1","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"The UC system calculates GPA using its own formula based specifically on 10th and 11th-grade A-G coursework.The "}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"1d9656be4cdc","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"609b140b049a","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"University of Michigan is particularly sensitive to course rigor and demonstrated interest alongside GPA"}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"2b1400a8c2d3","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"504123a668d2","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"If you are applying out of state to these flagship universities, expect even tighter competition. In-state applicants often receive an advantage in GPA thresholds."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"493b90ddeae5","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"04a5a2b4bdeb","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Moderately Selective Colleges and State Universities"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h3"},{"_key":"5f8389719b69","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"1a9e0fe5b1ab","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"This tier includes many public and private universities. They admit a meaningful share of applicants. They still maintain competitive standards."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"9a65ed320a5e","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"c090d3ac5bc1","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Typical GPA range for admission: 3.0 to 3.7"}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"d98d3e1a8b73","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"fe5d12b26673","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Many schools in this tier use holistic review. This means a strong GPA, solid extracurriculars, and good essays can make a significant difference."}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"95cd013dc9f0","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"4c330d44e286","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Some state universities in this range require a minimum GPA of 2.5, weighted for consideration"}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"fcc83aab7d71","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"1041773a923e","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Schools in this tier are often excellent options for students who have a strong profile outside GPA alone."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"bd40ca5a7d25","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"e7b85a1a3d1e","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Less Selective Colleges and Open-Enrollment Schools"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h3"},{"_key":"d28d60071190","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"e1c0aa88f9b3","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Not every college uses GPA as a hard barrier to admission."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"b50b759ec395","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"9ef6df98192e","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Minimum GPA requirements in this tier typically range from 2.0 to 2.5"}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"7ad91686e7b3","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"e538d67b0fef","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Some institutions accept students with a 2.0 GPA (a C average). Community colleges often have open enrollment. They may not require a minimum GPA."}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"122f5f92ddbb","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"a4e847bf868e","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"These schools tend to emphasize motivation, program fit, and future potential over past grades"}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"ec755d9c7586","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"2fbd1a0a0fa7","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Starting at a community college is a legitimate and often smart pathway. Students who earn a strong GPA at a community college can transfer to four-year universities. Some highly selective schools offer dedicated transfer programs."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"71109cabd926","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"31a6d38cfcea","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Minimum GPA vs Competitive GPA"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h2"},{"_key":"686e82fab714","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"1021f500f9ff","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Many students confuse these."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"ab93b02fd99b","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"ac667ba7d60f","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Minimum GPA"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h3"},{"_key":"cba7a67185fa","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"af3cfbe0dc60","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"The lowest GPA required to apply."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"2e573f958d7e","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"b293d41f50e3","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Competitive GPA"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h3"},{"_key":"96e6c7d9dd02","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"1bb1b7633a4c","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Admitted students commonly have this GPA."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"5809239faefa","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"0213b76d90cf","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Meeting minimum requirements does not guarantee admission."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"88c53e609fbd","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"9d402dcf5d84","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"How GPA Affects College Admissions"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h2"},{"_key":"7360847471c6","_type":"image","alt":"College Admission Office Board","asset":{"_id":"image-4a04a6ee59756136f1b73842b20e0ef819a0e0cd-1800x1200-webp","metadata":{"dimensions":{"_type":"sanity.imageDimensions","aspectRatio":1.5,"height":1200,"width":1800},"lqip":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},"url":"https://cdn.sanity.io/images/djth6w3n/production/4a04a6ee59756136f1b73842b20e0ef819a0e0cd-1800x1200.webp"},"caption":"College Admission Office ","markDefs":null},{"_key":"a3a80ad03460","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"3c20278550d5","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Admissions offices usually evaluate:"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"5b6ec4741de6","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"6b9859af32ce","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"GPA"}],"level":1,"listItem":"number","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"964e1f585199","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"a7286dd3c221","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Course rigor"}],"level":1,"listItem":"number","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"b4975429726f","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"58b4f255ecae","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Test scores (if required)"}],"level":1,"listItem":"number","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"4473aba31dbc","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"3281a2ef935e","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Essays"}],"level":1,"listItem":"number","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"d53d17ffa363","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"fc41f05940bc","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Activities"}],"level":1,"listItem":"number","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"4ead8d5ebc3d","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"49f50ae30d94","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Recommendations"}],"level":1,"listItem":"number","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"5a72d0c0ed6c","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"42b084707510","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"A slightly lower GPA combined with strong overall performance can still produce excellent outcomes."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"123c79af436b","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"29e01dfa38f8","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Test-Optional Admissions and GPA"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"h2"},{"_key":"3b0db1a24677","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"8b8c7e05f28c","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"At test-optional schools:"}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"e0b6439b62d8","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"b63302e5f04b","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"GPA often becomes more important."}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"d3f68b5779d8","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"5644c485106e","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Academic consistency matters."}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"1099706808cb","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"c2eae0c824ef","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Strong coursework can offset missing scores."}],"level":1,"listItem":"bullet","markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"8a44419d5015","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"18fd1f645d78","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"Always check each university's latest admissions policy."}],"markDefs":[],"style":"normal"},{"_key":"0aca7af47f64","_type":"block","children":[{"_key":"5909b186cb11","_type":"span","marks":[],"text":"What If Your GPA Is Lower Than Yo